  "review_notes": [
    "*the captains over thousands* renders the rectum anarthrously, so the article on הָאֲלָפִים takes the fronted *the* and the construct is left bare (rule 29); *the captains of the host* writes a *the* for each word, so nothing is fronted there.",
    "*houses* is the head noun the ASV supplies for the written הָאָבוֹת to stand on as a possessive and joins that noun's unit under rule 31; the ASV's italic corroborates the supply and decides nothing (rule 7)."
  ]
